    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.iii.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And Procne is to this day flitting about, lamenting; and her sister of Athens shrills with her tongue cut out.",
    "chunk_index": 39,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.iii.s12",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.iii.s12",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For what need is there of speaking of the goad of Œdipus, and the murder of Laius, and the marrying his mother, and the mutual slaughter of those who were at once his brothers and his sons?",
    "chunk_index": 40,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.iv.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.iv.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And your public assemblies I have come to hate. For there are excessive banquetings, and subtle flutes which provoke to lustful movements, and useless and luxurious anointings, and crowning with garlands.",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.iv.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.iv.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "With such a mass of evils do you banish shame; and ye fill your minds with them, and are carried away by intemperance, and indulge as a common practice in wicked and insane fornication.",
    "chunk_index": 42,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.iv.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.iv.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And this further I would say to you, why are you, being a Greek, indignant at your son when he imitates Jupiter, and rises against you and defrauds you of your own wife?",
    "chunk_index": 43,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.iv.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.iv.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Why do you count him your enemy, and yet worship one that is like him? And why do you blame your wife for living in unchastity, and yet honour Venus with shrines?",
    "chunk_index": 44,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.iv.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.iv.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If indeed these things had been related by others, they would have seemed to be mere slanderous accusations, and not truth. But now your own poets sing these things, and your histories noisily publish them.",
    "chunk_index": 45,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Henceforth, ye Greeks, come and partake of incomparable wisdom, and be instructed by the Divine Word, and acquaint yourselves with the King immortal; and do not recognise those men as heroes who slaughter whole nations.",
    "chunk_index": 46,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For our own Ruler, the Divine Word, who even now constantly aids us, does not desire strength of body and beauty of feature, nor yet the high spirit of earth’s nobility,",
    "chunk_index": 47,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "but a pure soul, fortified by holiness, and the watchwords of our King, holy actions, for through the Word power passes into the soul.",
    "chunk_index": 48,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "O trumpet of peace to the soul that is at war! O weapon that puttest to flight terrible passions! O instruction that quenches the innate fire of the soul!",
    "chunk_index": 49,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The Word exercises an influence which does not make poets: it does not equip philosophers nor skilled orators, but by its instruction it makes mortals immortal, mortals gods; and from the earth transports them to the realms above Olympus.",
    "chunk_index": 50,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Come, be taught; become as I am, for I, too, was as ye are. These have conquered me—the divinity of the instruction, and the power of the Word:",
    "chunk_index": 51,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for as a skilled serpent-charmer lures the terrible reptile from his den and causes it to flee, so the Word drives the fearful passions of our sensual nature from the very recesses of the soul;",
    "chunk_index": 52,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks#PsJust.OrGr.v.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-justin-discourse-to-the-greeks",
    "canonical_ref": "PsJust.OrGr.v.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "first driving forth lust, through which every ill is begotten—hatreds, strife, envy, emulations, anger, and such like. Lust being once banished, the soul becomes calm and serene.",
    "chunk_index": 53,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 200,
    "date_range": [
      150,
      300
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
